From 62d286df9fe363f0a0c82c04efb511e5411136f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:37:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(display): keep a copy of every image the model saw

Hermes stores the exact bytes of each image it gives the model (vision_analyze on either path, tool results that carry images, images a user sends natively), content-addressed by sha256 with a capped JPEG thumbnail, under HERMES_HOME/seen_images (400 days, 4 GiB). The tool or user row's display_metadata.seen_images lists the ids and tool.complete carries them. GET /api/seen-images/{id} serves a copy by id only, with the dashboard token check. A client can then show the image the model saw when its file is gone, outside the chat folder, on another machine or a subagent's.
